<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Awaji Island</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Awaji Island is the largest island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>'s Inland Sea, lying between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/honshu">Honshu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shikoku">Shikoku</a> and now part of Hyogo Prefecture. In Japanese mythology it is the first island created by the gods Izanagi and Izanami. Added to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokushima">Tokushima</a> domain of the Hachisuka family in 1615, it was separated from it after a violent dispute with the Inada family, its local governors, in 1870, and it is now linked to the mainland by the Akashi Kaikyo Bridge.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/awaji-island.jpg" alt="Awaji Island" width="320" height="353" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pinqui · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Awaji-island_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
